From 730ab0667bff7841c95563672c4757269d7cacde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Khairislamov <robertkhairislamov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 16:27:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [video_core,common] ARM Immortalis-G720 TBDR optimizations
 and crash fixes

TBDR rendering optimizations for ARM Mali/Immortalis and Qualcomm Adreno GPUs:
- Replace per-image VkImageMemoryBarrier with single VkMemoryBarrier on TBDR
- Narrow pipeline stage masks to avoid unnecessary tile cache flushes
- Add EARLY_FRAGMENT_TESTS to subpass self-dependency for TBDR tile overlap
- Reduce VMA block size to 32MB for mobile SoC memory efficiency
- Add ARM driver to demote reorder list for redundant fragment reduction

Crash fixes for missing Vulkan features on ARM (Immortalis-G720 MC12):
- Graceful degradation for 8 missing features (dualSrcBlend, logicOp, etc.)
- Pipeline creation guards: polygonMode, logicOp, dualSrcBlend, vertex divisor
- Try-catch around vkCreateGraphicsPipelines with draw call skip on failure
- Relaxed limits validation (maxViewports=1, maxClipDistances=0) on ARM

Memory stability fixes:
- host_memory: bounds-check Map/Unmap/Protect instead of fatal assert on overflow
- nvmap: fix pin count going negative (clamp to 0, prevent invalid handle state)
- nvmap: fix wrong handle checked during SMMU eviction (freeHandleDesc not handle_description)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
